# U-Boot environment location for the Umea QC01x (Goke GK7102C devkit).
#
# The vendor U-Boot partition is 320 KiB, i.e. its own 256 KiB plus a 64 KiB
# environment slot at 0x40000; the kernel partition starts at 0x50000, so an
# environment here cannot be larger than 64 KiB. mk-nor-image.sh writes a
# matching, CRC-valid environment into that slot.
#
# It is shipped rather than left to uboot-tools' env autodetect because the
# slot starts out erased: U-Boot reports "bad CRC, using default environment",
# detect_env() finds nothing to cache, and every fw_printenv/fw_setenv fails
# with "Cannot parse config file '/etc/fw_env.config'". That leaves wlandev/
# wlanssid/wlanpass, ptz_control/ptz_gpio and upgrade unreadable, and leaves
# gpio-motors without a pin list.
#
# device	offset		env_size
/dev/mtd0	0x40000		0x10000
